1
00:00:17,055 --> 00:00:22,020
Mine eyes have seen the glory
of the coming of the Lord:

2
00:00:22,103 --> 00:00:26,925
He is trampling out the vintage
where the grapes of wrath are stored;

3
00:00:26,969 --> 00:00:31,754
He hath loosed the fateful lightning
of His terrible swift sword:

4
00:00:31,812 --> 00:00:35,165
His truth is marching on.

5
00:00:37,014 --> 00:00:40,929
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

6
00:00:41,296 --> 00:00:44,861
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

7
00:00:45,212 --> 00:00:49,075
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

8
00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:52,893
His truth is marching on.

9
00:01:01,801 --> 00:01:06,850
I have seen Him in the watch-fires
of a hundred circling camps,

10
00:01:06,892 --> 00:01:11,754
They have builded Him an altar
in the evening dews and damps;

11
00:01:11,807 --> 00:01:16,646
I can read His righteous sentence
by the dim and flaring lamps:

12
00:01:16,913 --> 00:01:20,553
His day is marching on.

13
00:01:21,991 --> 00:01:25,801
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

14
00:01:26,095 --> 00:01:29,819
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

15
00:01:30,227 --> 00:01:33,867
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

16
00:01:34,075 --> 00:01:37,785
His day is marching on.

17
00:01:55,374 --> 00:02:00,545
I have read a fiery gospel writ
in burnished rows of steel:

18
00:02:00,679 --> 00:02:05,806
"As ye deal with my contemners,
so with you my grace shall deal;

19
00:02:06,015 --> 00:02:11,065
Let the Hero, born of woman,
crush the serpent with his heel,

20
00:02:11,379 --> 00:02:14,900
Since God is marching on."

21
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:20,503
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

22
00:02:20,848 --> 00:02:24,486
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

23
00:02:24,901 --> 00:02:28,736
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

24
00:02:28,904 --> 00:02:32,741
Since God is marching on.

25
00:02:49,255 --> 00:02:54,246
He has sounded forth the trumpet
that shall never call retreat;

26
00:02:54,476 --> 00:02:59,093
He is sifting out the hearts of men
before His judgment-seat:

27
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:04,092
Oh, be swift, my soul, to answer Him!
be jubilant, my feet!

28
00:03:04,263 --> 00:03:07,868
Our God is marching on.

29
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:13,260
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

30
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:17,332
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

31
00:03:17,791 --> 00:03:21,604
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

32
00:03:21,771 --> 00:03:25,561
Our God is marching on.

33
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:39,431
In the beauty of the lilies
Christ was born across the sea,

34
00:03:39,518 --> 00:03:44,276
With a glory in His bosom
that transfigures you and me:

35
00:03:44,332 --> 00:03:48,972
As He died to make men holy,
let us die to make men free,

36
00:03:49,039 --> 00:03:52,428
While God is marching on.

37
00:03:54,069 --> 00:03:58,091
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

38
00:03:58,385 --> 00:04:02,274
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

39
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:06,320
Glory, glory, hallelujah!

40
00:04:06,531 --> 00:04:10,303
While God is marching on.
